        {
          "project": "power-stone-subarasheese",
          "name_markdown": "[Power Stone (Subarasheese)](https://github.com/Subarasheese/powerstone-decomp)",
          "images": [
            {
              "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libretro-thumbnails/Sega_-_Dreamcast/master/Named_Boxarts/Power%20Stone%20%28USA%29.png",
              "alt": "US Dreamcast Power Stone front cover showing Edward Falcon reaching forward with other fighters behind him",
              "width": 100
            }
          ],
          "notes_markdown": "Work-in-progress C reconstruction of the USA Dreamcast release T-1201N, V1.001. Requires your own supported GDI disc and track files, Python, a Katana SDK and the documented SHC toolchain; Docker is the default, with a local Linux x86-64/wibo alternative. Byte-matching C units are distinct from generated and hand-written equivalent C checked against test cases; coverage is uneven and equivalence tests do not establish complete behavioral recovery. The matching baseline retains original assembly, while separate targets build experimental C-based Dreamcast executables and disc images. This is not a native PC port. [The README describes its AI-oriented, agentic reconstruction workflow](https://github.com/Subarasheese/powerstone-decomp#the-steps). Formerly named pwrstn-decomp.",
          "completion_percent": null,
          "completion_qualifier": "",
          "completion_metric": "completion",
          "ports": [],
          "project_types": [
            {
              "name": "Decompilation",
              "url": "https://github.com/Subarasheese/powerstone-decomp"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "project": "marvel-vs-capcom-2-gibletto",
          "name_markdown": "[Marvel vs. Capcom 2: New Age of Heroes (NAOMI and Dreamcast)](https://github.com/gibletto/mvc2-naomi-dc)",
          "images": [
            {
              "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/libretro-thumbnails/Sega_-_Dreamcast/master/Named_Boxarts/Marvel%20vs.%20Capcom%202%20%28USA%29.png",
              "alt": "Marvel vs. Capcom 2 USA Dreamcast cover art",
              "width": 100
            }
          ],
          "notes_markdown": "One source tree reconstructs the NAOMI export (mvsc2) and US (mvsc2u) program ROMs and the USA Dreamcast executable and character overlays. The [README](https://github.com/gibletto/mvc2-naomi-dc#readme) confirms Claude use and describes matching program builds with original Hitachi tools and Sega SDK libraries; most SDK modules remain precompiled, and several arcade blocks are extracted from the user's ROM. Matching programs do not imply a rebuilt complete disc or wholly reconstructed assets. Published executable, overlay and SDK hashes are not complete-disc hashes.",
          "completion_percent": null,
          "completion_qualifier": "",
          "completion_metric": "completion",
          "ports": [
            {
              "name": "MVC2 native ports",
              "url": "https://github.com/gibletto/mvc2-naomi-dc/tree/main/ports",
              "platforms": [
                "Windows",
                "Nintendo 3DS"
              ],
              "description_markdown": "Decompilation-based ports of both arcade and Dreamcast versions. Requires the user's own MAME mvsc2 set or USA Dreamcast disc data. Windows is 32-bit; 32-bit ARM Linux is buildable but untested, so it is not listed as a verified runtime target. Some library calls remain stubs. Old 3DS arcade mode requires the CIA memory mode; the 3DS sound path disables the AICA DSP. See the port documentation for setup and limitations.",
              "project_types": [
                "Native port"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "project_types": [
            {
              "name": "Matching decompilation",
